# One Tor, no pinned exit country. Pinning one with `ExitNodes {jp} StrictNodes 1`
# works, but it shrinks the set of relays the circuit can use, weakens what Tor
# is for, and fails outright when that country has no exit available. A country
# is what the VPN exits are for; this is for the other thing.

# Loopback, and loopback means something precise here: privoxy shares this
# container's network namespace, so it reaches the tunnel without the tunnel
# being reachable by anything else on the exits network. The HTTP front is the
# only way in.
SocksPort 9050
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy reject *

# For `SIGNAL NEWNYM` (a new circuit) in phase 3. Cookie authentication, and
# the port is never published: whoever wants it goes through `docker exec`, so
# no control secret has to live on the host where the agent could read it.
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
Log notice stdout
